cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Video Reverse Engineer, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "Video Reverse Engineer (editast)"
abstract: >-
  Video Reverse Engineer is an open-source, offline Python tool and CLI that
  reverse-engineers a finished video edit (TikTok, Instagram Reels, YouTube
  Shorts, film trailers) into a structured, timestamped Edit AST: every cut,
  transition, camera move, speed ramp, flash, colour effect and caption,
  aligned to the music's BPM, beats and drops. The AST can be exported as
  JSON, a readable text language (EditScript) and an interactive HTML report,
  and re-rendered as a template with new footage and music.
authors:
  - given-names: Pranav
    family-names: T
repository-code: "https://github.com/Pranav-Conova/video-reverse-engineer"
url: "https://github.com/Pranav-Conova/video-reverse-engineer"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - video analysis
  - video editing
  - reverse engineering
  - shot boundary detection
  - transition detection
  - beat tracking
  - music-video synchronization
  - abstract syntax tree
  - short-form video
